# L §5.18 (round 12) `check e == f`: "ok, or differs: e = …, f = … and, where e - f is defined (§3.2, §4.2), the
# difference e − f". Two texts have no difference (c1); two keys of one index differ by an int, "the difference of their
# positions (for an integer or period index, of the integers or periods)" (L §4.2): 2026-03 − 2026-01 = 2 (c2); two
# dates have none, date - date is undefined (L §4.2: days_between) (c3). (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.18, writer 5's
# T-86.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input a: text
input m1: key months
input d1: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = "x"
  m1 = 2026-01
  d1 = 2026-01-05

ask c1: check a == "y"
ask c2: check 2026-03 == m1
ask c3: check d1 == 2026-01-06
=== expect
c1: differs: a = "x", "y" = "y"
  cut 2026-10-18
c2: differs: 2026-03 = 2026-03, m1 = 2026-01, difference 2
  cut 2026-10-18
c3: differs: d1 = 2026-01-05, 2026-01-06 = 2026-01-06
  cut 2026-10-18
